  "mathematical_findings": [
    {
      "id": "local-ring-and-root-difference-valuation",
      "response_lines": [
        7,
        35,
        115,
        177
      ],
      "classification": "valid_structural_bridge",
      "reason": "The shifted prime-power cyclotomic polynomial is Eisenstein over Z_p, so O=Z_p[ζ] is a DVR with uniformizer ζ−1 and residue F_p. For u−v=p^s b with p∤b, the geometric quotient is a local unit. Factoring Φ_(p^(r−s))(1)=p and comparing valuations gives vπ(ζ^u−ζ^v)=p^s, with the correct ramification normalization."
    },
    {
      "id": "all-minor-unit-factor",
      "response_lines": [
        150,
        195
      ],
      "classification": "valid_baseline_and_extension",
      "reason": "The alternant divided by Vandermonde has integral coefficients and all-one value ∏(b_j−b_i)/∏j!. Every chosen row subset has m≤p and distinct residues, so this value is a p-unit; every root evaluates to one modulo π. Negative row exponents are handled by a common shift that multiplies by a unit. Thus every minor has exactly the asserted valuation, and the necessity witness using nodes 1 and a primitive p-th root is correct."
    },
    {
      "id": "exact-zero-set-and-all-active-coefficients",
      "response_lines": [
        39,
        52,
        179,
        195,
        231,
        241
      ],
      "classification": "valid_baseline_and_extension",
      "reason": "Invertibility of every square restriction proves the original zero bound and k-term bound. The t-node vanishing space has dimension k−t, and each unwanted new node imposes a proper hyperplane. Each coordinate-zero condition is also proper because the deleted-row t-node matrix retains rank t. Finite-union avoidance therefore realizes every t≤k−1 zero set with all coefficients active. The projective uniqueness at t=k−1 and return to the original three-term domain are valid."
    },
    {
      "id": "smith-and-finite-precision-classification",
      "response_lines": [
        54,
        111,
        197,
        209
      ],
      "classification": "valid_R3_structure",
      "reason": "Over a DVR, each determinantal ideal valuation is the minimum valuation of its minors. The proved minor formula makes this exactly Δ_m, so the successive differences are all Smith exponents and determine the coker/free part. Invertible row/column reductions preserve the finite-precision map: the image size and the Ub divisibility/zero conditions are precisely those of π^λ diagonal multiplication modulo π^q. The full-column exponents 0,…,k−1 follow by choosing m distinct mod-p column residues."
    },
    {
      "id": "collision-tree-dynamic-program",
      "response_lines": [
        211,
        229
      ],
      "classification": "valid_complete_computation_mechanism",
      "reason": "At each p-adic residue-tree level, α_0=1 and α_h=p^h−p^(h−1) charge binom(t,2) for pairs still coinciding. A pair of valuation s receives exactly Σ_(h=0)^s α_h=p^s. Capacity-constrained leaf states and independent child minimization therefore compute the defining Δ_m exactly, including sparse J and repeated residue levels."
    }
  ],
